                <pb facs="0250" n="904" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg904"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in 2 in No. 219.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Captain Beyer to the post adjutant, Ringgold
                        Barracks.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Camp Company C</hi>, 9<hi rendition="#small-caps">th
                                Cavalry</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Roma,
                            Texas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1875-03-01"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">March</hi> 1, 1875</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">To the <hi rendition="#small-caps">Post Adjutant</hi>,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ringgold Barracks, Texas:</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that during the
                    month of February, 1875, Company C, Ninth Cavalry, performed the usual scouting
                    and patrol duties assigned to it.</p>
                <p>The following scouts were made during the month:</p>
                <p>Captain Beyer, Ninth Cavalry, with two (2) sergeants, two (2) corporals, one (1)
                    trumpeter, one (1) blacksmith, and seventeen (17) privates, left this camp on
                    the morning of February 10, 1875, on a scout through the following counties or
                    portions of same, Starr, Zapata, Duval, and Webb, returning to Roma, Texas,
                    February 21, 1875; distance marched about three hundred miles.</p>
                <p>Patrols were frequently sent out during the month, who patrolled the Rio Grande
                    between here and Carizo.</p>
                <p>No report of any cattle-stealing or of depredations committed have reached
                    me.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>C. D. BEYER,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Captain</hi> 9<hi
                            rendition="#italic">th Cavalry, Commanding Company
                    C</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
